  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In the 1960s the rocket engineer Wernher von Braun reportedly told Time magazine where the point of neutral gravity lies between the Earth and the moon, the spot where the two pulls cancel out, and gave about double the official figure. The comedian Kurt Metzger tells this to Michels, passing on what he read from the author Joseph P. Farrell. If true, it would mean the official numbers about the moon's gravity were not the whole story."
